  "notes": [
    "This is a dated acceptance snapshot, not a guarantee of future upstream availability.",
    "Ad-hoc checks on the same day, with the same build: Codex CLI 0.164 completed a real file task through its remote compaction (capabilities.remote_compaction = \"v2\", which sends compaction_trigger) with gemini-3-flash and claude-sonnet-4-6, and through its default local compaction with claude-sonnet-4-6.",
    "Antigravity rejects requests that end with a model turn for every model (\"Requests ending with a model turn are not supported\"; Claude: \"does not support assistant message prefill\"). An empty user turn is treated as missing. agy2api appends a \"Continue.\" user turn, and the models continued the assistant text.",
    "Antigravity gates new models by client version: with User-Agent antigravity/1.0.0, gemini-3.8-flash-high returned 404 while 2.22.0 and later succeeded. The service reported antigravity/2.26.0 from the release manifest during this run.",
    "Upstream session IDs did not affect caching: Gemini reused its prefix cache across different session IDs, and Claude showed no cache hits with or without the same session ID.",
    "Antigravity answers 429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED to any request whose system prompt contains Claude Code's x-anthropic-billing-header line or its Claude Agent SDK identity line. agy2api forwards the prompt unchanged.",
    "Gemini 2.5 Pro remained unavailable (MODEL_CAPACITY_EXHAUSTED).",
    "Stop sequences truncate text, but exact Anthropic stop_reason/stop_sequence metadata remains partial because upstream exposes only STOP.",
    "Token values are sampled response usage, not total usage across every call in a scenario.",
    "No credential values, project identifiers, generated image bytes, or opaque replay signatures are included."
